ith that Pokémon collector... Now the police is all up in our business."1You know this could disturb our plans for..."^Oh, hello \V[25]. We were just talking about you. You did very well on your last mission."�That run-in with the police was unfortunate, but you handled it with the finesse of a Team Rocket Admin. I'm pleased with your work so far."dI have a new mission to assign you to. This'll be your most important mission up to this point."-Come and see me as soon as you're ready."oApparently, some kid teamed up with the Gym Leader and infiltrated the hideout... No, that can't be right."0Why does the captain like you more than me?"4Man, I can't believe we messed up that mission.",Archer is tough with us, but he's fair."PYou were pretty good on that mission. But of course, I had the hardest job."NHumph.. I shouldn't have let you take the lead on that mission, \V[25]..."Who goes there!?"8Okay, looks like you're with Team Rocket. Go ahead.".Hey! This is a private property. Go away!"-Hmm... You look a little bit familiar..."%Nah, I must be imagining things!")Which floor would you like to go to?"M<b>Confidential</b>\nTeam Rocket Celadon Division: Operational Directive"Take a look?"><b>Subject:</b> Strategic Priorities for Celadon Division"xWe're hitting \C[5]Pinkan Island\C[0] to secure a rumored mythical Pokémon that is believed to be highly valuable.".This operation serves two key objectives:"n<b>Revenue Generation:</b> Selling the Pokémon will secure vital funding for Team Rocket's larger goals."�<b>Strategic Diversion:</b> The heist will divert law enforcement attention away from Operation 3F, ensuring its smooth execution."Make sure that all agents are properly trained and briefed about the importance of the mission - failure is not an option.")<b>For the glory of Team Rocket.</b>"JHey! What do you think you're doing? This is a confidential document!"MWho are you? \V[25]? I assume you're transfering from Cerulean City huh?"�Hmm.. you'll do the job. But I warn you, don't expect me to be as gentle as Petrel. Things are a lot more serious here in the big city."SAre you still up for it? Well then here's your first mission under my command."VLately, the boss has asked us to recruit a lot of new grunts for an upcoming job."DWe've had to recruit a lot of new grunts for the Silph Co. job."But our Pokémon supplier hasn't been able to keep up. I need you to go catch some new Pokémon to give to the new grunts."VGo out in the outskirts of the city and catch 3 Pokémon with these Rocket Balls."TMake sure that you use the Rocket Balls and that all of them at least Level 20."=Have you caught all the Pokémon for the new grunts yet?"?Is this one of the Pokémon you caught for the new grunts?""\PN handed over the Pokémon.")That was the last of them! Good job."<Alright, well here's your cut for this first mission.\G"\G\PN received $\V[312]"�You used so many Rocket Balls that I can't give you a payment for this mission. You're lucky that I'm not making you pay out of pocket."hI can't deny that you're showing some potential. Come back when you're ready for your next mission."]Yes, it'll do perfectly. There are still \V[311] left to catch. Do you have another one?"AYou still need to catch \V[311] Pokémon for the new grunts."VMake sure that they're at least level 20 and that you catch them in Rocket Balls."QYou've used all of our Rocket Balls inventory... You wasted every last ball!"bI really hope you have other talents because you're remarkably useless as a Pokémon catcher."5Let's hope you do better on your next mission..."XHumph... Fine, but I'll have to dock your payout to make up for these wasted balls."Grunts!"Ready, captain!"On your command!"XGrunts, now that you've all received your Pokémon, I have a mission to assign you."�Lately. the Game Corner's supply of TMs has been runnning low. As you know, the Game Corner is vital to finance our operations here in Celadon City..."lNow, it just so happens that the Celadon Department Store is expecting a new shipment of TMs this week."wI will need you to intercept the shipment, then to pose as the delivery person and deliver these fake TMs instead."^Then, we'll keep all of the real TMs to ourselves and they'll be none the wiser. Fuhahah!"XThe shipment is expected to come through the \C[1]Underground Path\C[0] on Route 7."NThis will be the perfect place to intercept it without anyone seeing you."fI will need you three to stay posted there. You'll only get one chance at this, so don't miss it!""Go, now! Don't lose any time!"Understood!"Aye aye, captain!"Yes, captain!"Ready!".\GYou did very well on that last mission."P\GHere are you cuts. I'm very pleased with the way this team is shaping up."\G\PN obtained $10,000"cAnd as a bonus for a job well done, I'll let you each keep one of the TMs that we intercepted.":\PN, you had the hardest job so you can choose first."RKeep up the good work. \V[25], please come and see me when you have a moment."}Grunts, I am disappointed. This was a simple mission that would've been very profitable for us, but you couldn't handle it..."EYou need to take your missions a lot more seriously from now on."Sorry boss..."#We won't disappoint you again!"n\V[25], please come and see me when you have a moment. I have a new mission that I want to assign you to."xGood job intercepting that package. Now all that's left to do is to deliver the counterfeit TMs to the Dept. Store."hI need you to intercept the shipment, then to pose as the delivery person and deliver the fake TMs."\Go wait with the other grunts. You'll only get once chance at intercepting the package."\V[25]!"UEven though your last mission was a failure, I've been impressed by your skills."RAnd so I've decided to assign you a more important mission for your next one.">Very good, \V[25]. I am very happy with your work so far."mYou have shown that you can be trusted, and so this next mission will be one that requires more finesse."tThere's this... collector from Joht