 at the moment."PHe went to do some field work in Route 1. He shouldn't be back in too long."#I'm professor Oak's assistant."OWe do a lot of research on Pokemon fusion and the possibilities it offers."OTake these! They'll come in handy for recording Pokémon in your Pokédex!"<Gramps told me to wait for him here. Stop bothering me!"7It's not fair! Why don't I ever get to pick first?"Re-randomize Pokémon?""The Pokédex was re-shuffled."7It is time for you two to set out on your journey.",Go and grab your pokemon off the table."4No fair! Why does \PN always get to pick first?"*You'll get one too, Blue. Be patient!"$The Pokeballs are on the table."(Go ahead, choose one. Don't be shy."So you chose \V[5] uh?"XWell gramps just got me one of these new DNA Splicer they were talking about on TV."?So I guess I'll take the other two and try it out on them!"!I can do that, right gramps?"4Of course! Here, I'll show you how to use them."vDNA splicers can be used to combine the DNA of two Pokemon together to create an entirely new species of Pokemon."PI would give you some as well, \PN but unfortunately,this was my last pair!"Good luck on your journey!":\PN before you leave, could you please do me a favor?"HI need you to pick up a parcel at Viridian City's PokéMart for me."AIt's just down the road, but I forgot to pick it up earlier.")\PN, could you please do me a favor?"CIt's not very far from here and it would help me a great deal."LOh \PN! How is my old Pokémon doing? Well, it seems to like you a lot."%What? You have something for me?" \PN delivered Oak's Parcel.";Ah! This is the custom PokéBall I ordered! Thank you!"nAnd I can see they gave you some DNA Splicers as well. How convenient since you've just become a trainer!"HBut of course, you'll need a second Pokémon before you can use it."VHere, I'll give you some Poké Balls so you can catch some Pokémon to try it on!"wYou can always defuse your Pokémon if you don't like the result, but it will lose some experience in the process."GOh and did you get some DNA Splicers while you were there as well?"PYou didn't? Oh, that's no problem. You can always return to buy some later!" There's also another thing."FI forgot to give you your Pokédex before you headed out earlier!"\PN obtained the Pokédex!"3I already gave my grandson his before he left."lThe Pokédex automatically records data on Pokémon you've seen or caught! It's a hi-tech encyclopedia!"~There are now over 200,000 species of Pokémon thanks to Pokémon Fusion, so I cannot possibly expect you to complete it."LBut you should still try to catch as many different species as you can!"<Now go! Your journey to the Pokémon League starts now!":Did you talk to my colleague, Professor Elm in Johto?"mCongratulations on getting all of these Johto gym badges It isn't an easy task that you've accomplished!"�I have one more Pokémon to give you. You can have one of the starter Pokémon that are handed to new trainers in the Hoenn region." No, which one did you want?"oMy colleague Professor Elm in Johto came across some new information concerning the whereabouts of Mewtwo."JPlease go meet him at his lab in New Bark Town for more instructions!"]You can get there by heading West from Viridian City, past Route 26 and the Tohjo falls."XIt'll be a long journey, but nothing is too tough for the Pokémon League champion!";This is Professor Oak's Pokeball. Better not touch it!"This ball contains \V[5]."!Do you want to choose \V[5]?"6It's a complex looking sink. Better not touch it!"NThe screen shows a research paper that Professor Oak has been working on."/It's filled with complex scientific terms!"8I worked with Professor Oak designing the Pokédex."$It really is an amazing device!"Not so fast, \PN!"cLet's have a battle to see how much stronger a Pokémon gets when it's fused with another one!"?I don't believe it! How could my cool fused Pokemon lose!?"NPff... This Pokémon is completely worthless. I'll find some better ones!"$Ha! I always knew I was better!"aI'm going to catch some more Pokémon to see if I can get them to be stronger than this one."(Wait.. you didn't choose a Pokemon?"How is that even possible?"*Well never mind then. Smell ya later!"+Anyway, I'm off to collect gym badges."Smell ya later!"Yes"No"Treecko"Torchic"Mudkip[^":It's a complex looking document. Better not touch it!"/The shelves are filled with science books."7Don't leave now! You haven't chosen a Pokemon yet!"9It's a complex looking machine. Better not touch it!"Rerandomize starters?"Your wish is my command!"2There's nothing in here, what did you expect?")A soap opera is playing on the TV..."Better get going!"That's a TV.",Oh, were you looking for professor Oak?"-I'm afraid he isn't there at the moment."PHe went to do some field work in Route 1. He shouldn't be back in too long."#I'm professor Oak's assistant."OWe do a lot of research on Pokemon fusion and the possibilities it offers."OTake these! They'll come in handy for recording Pokémon in your Pokédex!"=Gramps told me to wait for him here.  Stop bothering me!"7It's not fair! Why don't I ever get to pick first?"Re-randomize Pokémon?""The Pokédex was re-shuffled."7It is time for you two to set out on your journey.",Go and grab your pokemon off the table."4No fair! Why does \PN always get to pick first?"*You'll get one too, Blue. Be patient!"$The Pokeballs are on the table."(Go ahead, choose one. Don't be shy."So you chose \V[5] uh?"XWell gramps just got me one of these new DNA Splicer they were talking about on TV."?So I guess I'll take the other two and try it out on them!"!I can do that, right gramps?"4Of course! Here, I'll show you how to use them."vDNA splicers can be used to combine the DNA of two Pokemon together to create an entirely new species of Pokemon."PI would give you some as well, \PN but unfortunately,this was my last pair!"Good luck on your journey!":\PN before you leave, could you please do me a favor?"HI need you to pick up a parcel at Viridian City's PokéMart fo