."/It's filled with complex scientific terms!"6It's a complex looking sink. Better not touch it!"8I worked with Professor Oak designing the Pokédex."$It really is an amazing device!"Not so fast, \PN!"cLet's have a battle to see how much stronger a Pokémon gets when it's fused with another one!"?I don't believe it! How could my cool fused Pokemon lose!?"NPff... This Pokémon is completely worthless. I'll find some better ones!"$Ha! I always knew I was better!"aI'm going to catch some more Pokémon to see if I can get them to be stronger than this one."(Wait.. you didn't choose a Pokemon?"How is that even possible?"*Well never mind then. Smell ya later!"+Anyway, I'm off to collect gym badges."Smell ya later!"Yes"No"Treecko"Torchic"Mudkip[^"9It's a complex looking machine. Better not touch it!":It's a complex looking document. Better not touch it!"7Don't leave now! You haven't chosen a Pokemon yet!"/The shelves are filled with science books."Rerandomize starters?"Your wish is my command!"=Gramps told me to wait for him here.  Stop bothering me!"7It's not fair! Why don't I ever get to pick first?",Oh, were you looking for professor Oak?"-I'm afraid he isn't there at the moment."PHe went to do some field work in Route 1. He shouldn't be back in too long."#I'm professor Oak's assistant."OWe do a lot of research on Pokemon fusion and the possibilities it offers."OTake these! They'll come in handy for recording Pokémon in your Pokédex!")A soap opera is playing on the TV..."Better get going!"That's a TV."2There's nothing in here, what did you expect?"Re-randomize Pokémon?""The Pokédex was re-shuffled.";This is Professor Oak's Pokeball. Better not touch it!"This ball contains \V[5]."!Do you want to choose \V[5]?"7It is time for you two to set out on your journey.",Go and grab your pokemon off the table."4No fair! Why does \PN always get to pick first?"*You'll get one too, Blue. Be patient!"$The Pokeballs are on the table."(Go ahead, choose one. Don't be shy."So y