okemon yet!"NThe screen shows a research paper that Professor Oak has been working on."/It's filled with complex scientific terms!"/The shelves are filled with science books.":It's a complex looking document. Better not touch it!"7It's a complex looking globe. Better not touch it!"oCynthia... If what you are saying is true, then it could only be caused by an immensely powerful Pokémon."~I have studied the Sinnoh myths extensively and I believe that there exist Pokémon that could excert this sort of power."?But this begs the question: Why Mt. Silver, of all places?"?Ah, \PN! I didn't hear you come in. It is good to see you!"pThis is Cynthia. She came all the way from the Sinnoh region to share a very interesting discovery with us."R\PN... Yes! I remember you from the Sinjoh Ruins. It's good to see you again."%\PN... I am pleased to meet you!"[So \PN, you got all the Johto badges too, huh? You really can't get enough, can't you?"�I figured you were something special when you beat me at the Pokémon League, but to think you'd get all the badges from Johto too... This is just something else!"yThere are very few trainers who can claim to have so many badges. It is quite the achievement. Congratulations, \PN!"�Cynthia's a League Champion just like you, you know? If you're looking for one final opponent to test your skills against, then she's probably it!"pOne day, we might get the chance to face off against each other, but for now we have more pressing matters."Yes, of course... Go on."qAs I was just telling Professor Oak, scientists from my home region have noticed odd readings on Mt. Silver."_As you approach the summit, it appears that the laws of physics start to behave strangely."qTime slows down and objects seem to be pulled inwards as if they were about to get sucked into a black hole."uThe scientists say that such a strange phenomenon could only be caused by a significant distortion in spacetime."�But the patterns are too irregular for it to be from natural causes. It's as if space and time were being deliberately manipulated by something..."�Of course there's only so much information we can obtain from instrument readings. That's why I came here to check it out in person!"�There are myths in the Sinnoh region that describe two legendary Pokémon that are able to alter the spatial and temporal dimensions respectively."GBut manipulating both time and space at once... That's unheard of!"vSince we might be dealing with something powerful, I asked \V[12] to come join me on my expedition to Mt. Silver."HIf it's a Pokémon, then I'm gonna catch it and I'll be unbeatable!"�\PN, would you like to join us? We do not know what we're up against so we could always use an experienced Pokémon trainer such as yourself."cGreat! You can come and meet us near the entrance to Mt. Silver so we can plan the expedition!"HIt's a long trek to the top of the mountain so we should leave now."$Thank you very much, professor.":\V[12], \PN, let's meet up at the base of Mt. Silver!"|Oh... That's disappointing. But of course, as a League Champion myself, I completely understand that you are very busy."PIt's a long trek to the top of the mountain so we should leave now, \V[12]."~\PN! If you change mind, please come and meet us near the base of Mt. Silver. We'll be prepping for the expedition there."?Thank you so much, professor. \V[12], let's go right away!"?It's a complex looking picture frame. Better not touch it!"<Gramps told me to wait for him here. Stop bothering me!"7It's not fair! Why don't I ever get to pick first?",Oh, were you looking for professor Oak?"-I'm afraid he isn't there at the moment."PHe went to do some field work in Route 1. He shouldn't be back in too long."OTake these! They'll come in handy for recording Pokémon in your Pokédex!"#I'm professor Oak's assistant."OWe do a lot of research on Pokemon fusion and the possibilities it offers.")A soap opera is playing on the TV..."Better get going!"That's a TV."2There's nothing in here, what did you expect?"7It's a complex looking plant. Better not touch it!"Re-randomize Pokémon?""The Pokédex was re-shuffled."o\V[12] and Cynthia went to Mt. Silver to prep for the expedition. You should join them as soon as you can!"ZI believe the way to Mt. Silver is through the gate that is just before Victory Road."^So the Pokémon on Mt. Silver bended timespace and took you three years into the future!?"JThis is truly one of the most astounding events I have ever heard of.";This is Professor Oak's Pokeball. Better not touch it!"6This ball contains Bulbasaur, the grass Pokémon."%Do you want to choose Bulbasaur?"'\f[\v[4]]This ball contains \V[5]."*\f[\v[4]]Do you want to choose \V[5]?"7It is time for you two to set out on your journey.",Go and grab your pokemon off the table."4No fair! Why does \PN always get to pick first?",You'll get one too, \V[12]. Be patient!"$The Pokeballs are on the table."(Go ahead, choose one. Don't be shy."So you chose \V[5] uh?"%In this case I'll take this one."XWell gramps just got me one of these new DNA Splicer they were talking about on TV."?So I guess I'll take the other two and try it out on them!"|Ah, yes. DNA splicers are used to combine the DNA of two Pokemon together to create an entirely new species of Pokemon."+It works on every Pokémon, of course."PI would give you some as well, \PN but unfortunately,this was my last pair!"Good luck on your journey!":\PN before you leave, could you please do me a favor?"HI need you to pick up a parcel at Viridian City's PokéMart for me."AIt's just down the road, but I forgot to pick it up earlier.")\PN, could you please do me a favor?"CIt's not very far from here and it would help me a great deal."LOh \PN! How is my old Pokémon doing? Well, it seems to like you a lot."%What? You have something for me?" \PN delivered Oak's Parcel.";Ah! This is the custom PokéBall I ordered! Thank you!"KAnd I can see they gave you some DNA Splicers as well. How convenient!"HBut of course, you'll need a second Pokémon before you can use it."VHere, I'll give you some Poké Balls so you can catch some Pokémon to try it on!"QYou can always unfuse your Pokémon if you don't like the result, of course."GOh and did you get some DNA Splicers while you were there as well?"PYou didn't? Oh, that's no problem. You can always return to buy some later!" There's also another thing."FI forgot to give you your Pokédex before you headed out earlier!"\PN obtained the Pokédex!"3I already gave my grandson his before he left."lThe Pokédex automatically records data on Pokémon you've seen or caught! It's a hi-tech encyclopedia!"~There are now over 200,000 species of Pokémon thanks to Pokémon Fusion, so I cannot possibly expect you to complete it."LBut you should still try to catch as many different species as you can!"<Now go! Your journey to the Pokémon League starts now!":Did you talk to my colleague, Professor Elm in Johto?"mCongratulations on getting all of these Johto gym badges It isn't an easy task that you've accomplished!"�I have one more Pokémon to give you. You can have one of the starter Pokémon that are handed to new trainers in the Hoenn region." No, which one did you want?"oMy colleague Professor Elm in Johto came across some new information concerning the whereabouts of Mewtwo."JPlease go meet him at his lab in New Bark Town for more instructions!"kYou can get there by taking the train to Goldenrod from Saffron City and heading South To Azalea Town."DFrom there, just follow the road until you reach New Bark Town."XIt'll be a long journey, but nothing is too tough for the Pokémon League champion!"9It's a complex looking machine. Better not touch it!"6It's a complex looking sink. Better not touch it!"4This ball contains Squirtle, the water Pokemon."$Do you want to choose Squirtle?"4This ball contains Charmander the fire Pokemon."&Do you want to choose Charmander?"8I worked with Professor Oak designing the Pokédex."$It really is an amazing device!"`If it isn't the new Pokémon League Champion! Welcome home \PN, it's good to have you back."YEveryone in the Pokémon scientific community is very impressed by your achievement."�I have been talking with my colleague from the Johto region, professor Elm and he tasked me to give you a Pokémon to commemorate your victory."/Now, which one of those three do you want?"EGreat choice! I'm sure this Pokémon will be in excellent hands."@There is also another thing that my colleague mentionned..."9Are you familiar with the legendary Pokémon Mewtwo?"�It was created by some scientists in Cinnabar Island some time ago. But one day, it fled the mansion and hasn't been seen ever since."EIt is said to be one of the most powerful Pokémon in existance."yRecently, my colleague Professor Elm in Johto came across some new information concerning the whereabouts of Mewtwo."gHe says he'd need the assistance of a strong trainer, so I thought you'd be the perfect candidate."His lab is located in New Bark Town in the Johto region. It's a long way from here, but do you think you could pay him a visit?"oPlease! Professor Elm would greatly benefit from the field experience of a powerful trainer like yourself."!Won't you please reconsider?"}Great! Then it's settled. Go meet my colleague Professor Elm in New Bark Town and he'll give you some more instructions!"Not so fast, \PN!"cLet's have a battle to see how much stronger a Pokémon gets when it's fused with another one!"?I don't believe it! How could my cool fused Pokemon lose!?"NPff... This Pokémon is completely worthless. I'll find some better ones!"$Ha! I always knew I was better!"aI'm going to catch some more Pokémon to see if I can get them to be stronger than this one."(Wait.. you didn't choose a Pokemon?"How is that even possible?"*Well never mind then. Smell ya later!"+Anyway, I'm off to collect gym badges."Smell ya later!"Yes"No"Treecko"Torchic"Mudkip"Chikorita"Cyndaquil"Totodile"	Sure"Not really...[�";It's a complex looking bookshelf. Better not to