oesn't absorb much sunlight."YThis Berry is very big and sour. The juiciness of the pulp accentuates the sourness."rA small hint of spiciness lingers in the red granules surrounding this Berry. Their centers have a dry taste."fThough this small, delicately skinned Berry is blue in color, it dyes the mouth black when eaten."jBitter, but with a trace of sweetness, the Nanab Berry was the seventh to be discovered in the world."sThe potent mix of bitter and sour in this Berry seems to promote digestion. The flower is white and beautiful."dIt is said that when the sour skin is peeled, this spicy Berry can be crushed to make medicine."^When this sweetly spicy Berry's thick skin is peeled, many pieces of the fruit spill out."eThis Berry can be eaten as is or boiled to obtain an extract that adds a dash of flavor to food."dEven in places of constant rain and high humidity, this Berry's plant grows healthy and strong."[This somewhat-rare Berry projects an image of luxury, so it is favored as a gift item."XOne bite of this very tender Berry fills the mouth with its sweet and tangy flavor."eThis Berry is large and spicy. When eaten during the cold season, it warms the body from inside."uIts dryness is quite strong. As a result, its true deliciousness can't be appreciated by just eating one or two."fThe grown-up flavor and dreamy sweetness of this Berry make it a favorite of Pokémon everywhere."xEven though it is bitter, it should be eaten peel and all. The hair on the peel cleans the stomach from the inside."dThis Berry is quite sour overall, with the sourness especially concentrated at the pointed end."vSo spicy is the Spelon Berry that, Fire type or not, Pokémon will try to breathe fire after eating a single one."VThis Berry drifted from a faraway sea. It is now cultivated in the Sinnoh region."qA bounty of nature that is exceedingly sweet. The Berry is huge, with some discovered that exceed 20 inches."ZThis Berry is tremendously bitter. Just one bite is enough to instantly stop hiccups."lThis glossy and colorful Berry has a mouthwateringly delicious appearance. However, it is awfully sour."qThis Berry is said to have grown plentiful in the tropics of the past. It boasts an intensely hot spiciness."bThis Berry's flesh is dotted with countless tiny bubbles of air that keep it afloat in water."aEnergy from lightning strikes is drawn into the plant, making the Berries grow big and rich."xThis berry has a disagreeable "green" flavor and scent typical of vegetables. It is rich in health-promoting fiber."vThis Berry has a refreshing flavor that strikes a good balance of dryness and sourness. It tastes better chilled."]This Berry contains a substance that generates heat. It can even heat up a chilly heart."sThis Berry is a brilliant green on the outside. Inside, it is packed with a dry-flavored, black-colored flesh."XThe sweetness-laden pulp has just the hint of a hard-edged and fragrant bite to it."pThis Berry is said to be a new kind that is a cross of two Berries brought together by winds from far away."gThis Berry is said to sense human emotions for the way it swells roundly when a person approaches."rThe flower grows at the tip of this Berry. It attracts Bug Pokémon by letting its stringy petals stream out."uIt is often used for pickles because of its very dry flavor. It can also be eaten raw for its provocative taste."yConsidered to have a special power from the olden days, this Berry is sometimes dried and used as a good-luck charm."kIf a large enough volume of this Berry is boiled down, its bitterness fades away. It makes a good jam."tTiny hooks grow on the surface of this Berry. It latches on to Pokémon so it can be carried to far-off places."gThis Berry is very tough with a strong flavor. It was used to make medicine by people in the past."tThis Berry can be cored out and dried to make a whistle. Blowing through its hole makes an indescribable sound."_This Berry is surrounded by mystery. It is rumored to be imbued with the power of the sea."`This Berry is surrounded by mystery. It is rumored to be imbued with the power of the land."_This Berry is surrounded by mystery. It is rumored to be imbued with the power of the sky."iThis Berry is surrounded by mystery. It is rumored to be imbued with the power of all living things."uThis is a very, very mystifying Berry. There is no telling how it can be used, or what may happen if it is used."RThis is said to be a legendary Berry. Holding it supposedly brings great joy."tThis Berry is considered a mirage. It was said to be so strong that it had to be abandoned at the world's edge."dA completely enigmatic Berry. It apparently has the power of the stars that fill the night sky."qThis berry has a very dry flavor. It has the effect of making other food eaten at the same time taste sweet."QThe flesh underneath the Custap Berry's tough skin is sweet and creamy soft."gThe cluster of drupelets that make up this berry pop rhythmically if the berry is handled roughly."bIn days of old, people worked the top-shaped pieces of this Berry free and used them as toys."{The slight bitterness that cuts through the rich sweetness makes this Berry a perfect ingredient for adding an accent.[F"oThis bright red Berry is very spicy and has a provocative flavor. It blooms with delicate, pretty flowers."mThis Berry's thick skin and fruit are very tough and dry tasting. However, every bit of it can be eaten."rBecause of its hollow inside pocket, there isn't a lot to eat. What can be eaten is very sweet and delicious."fIf the leaves grow longer and curlier than average, this Berry will have a somewhat-bitter taste."pThis Berry's peel is hard, but the flesh inside is very juicy. It is distinguished by its bracing sourness."ZIt takes longer to grow than Berries such as Cheri. The smaller Berries taste better."rNature's gifts came together as one in this Berry. It has a wondrous mix of flavors that spread in the mouth."ZThe more this berry absorbs energy from sunlight, the more vividly colorful it grows."pThis Berry's gradual process of storing nutrients beneficial to Pokémon health causes it to mature slowly."[Sitrus came from the same family as Oran. It is larger and smoother tasting than Oran."vThis Berry is oddly shaped, appearing as if someone took a bite out of it. It is packed full of spicy substances."iIt is said that this Berry grew lumps to help Pokémon grip it, allowing propagation farther afield."aThis Berry progressively curves as it grows. The curvier the Berry, the sweeter and tastier."kThis Berry turns bitter toward the stem. The dainty flower it grows from doesn't absorb much sunlight."YThis Berry is very big and sour. The juiciness of the pulp accentuates the sourness."rA small hint of spiciness lingers in the red granules surrounding this Berry. Their centers have a dry taste."fThough this small, delicately skinned Berry is blue in color, it dyes the mouth black when eaten."jBitter, but with a trace of sweetness, the Nanab Berry was the seventh to be discovered in the world."sThe potent mix of bitter and sour in this Berry seems to promote digestion. The flower is white and beautiful."dIt is said that when the sour skin is peeled, this spicy Berry can be crushed to make medicine."^When this sweetly spicy Berry's thick skin is peeled, many pieces of the fruit spill out."eThis Berry can be eaten as is or boiled to obtain an extract that adds a dash of flavor to food."dEven in places of constant rain and high humidity, this Berry's plant grows healthy and strong."[This somewhat-rare Berry projects an image of luxury, so it is favored as a gift item."XOne bite of this very tender Berry fills the mouth with its sweet and tangy flavor."eThis Berry is large and spicy. When eaten during the cold season, it warms the body from inside."uIts dryness is quite strong. As a result, its true deliciousness can't be appreciated by just eating one or two."fThe grown-up flavor and dreamy sweetness of this Berry make it a favorite of Pokémon everywhere."xEven though it is bitter, it should be eaten peel and all. The hair on the peel cleans the stomach from the inside."dThis Berry is quite sour overall, with the sourness especially concentrated at the pointed end."vSo spicy is the Spelon Berry that, Fire type or not, Pokémon will try to breathe fire after eating a single one."VThis Berry drifted from a faraway sea. It is now cultivated in the Sinnoh region."qA bounty of nature that is exceedingly sweet. The Berry is huge, with some discovered that exceed 20 inches."ZThis Berry is tremendously bitter. Just one bite is enough to instantly stop hiccups."lThis glossy and colorful Berry has a mouthwateringly delicious appearance. However, it is awfully sour."qThis Berry is said to have grown plentiful in the tropics of the past. It boasts an intensely hot spiciness."bThis Berry's flesh is dotted with countless tiny bubbles of air that keep it afloat in water."aEnergy from lightning strikes is drawn into the plant, making the Berries grow big and rich."xThis berry has a disagreeable "green" flavor and scent typical of vegetables. It is rich in health-promoting fiber."vThis Berry has a refreshing flavor that strikes a good balance of dryness and sourness. It tastes better chilled."]This Berry contains a substance that generates heat. It can even heat up a chilly heart."sThis Berry is a brilliant green on the outside. Inside, it is packed with a dry-flavored, black-colored flesh."XThe sweetness-laden pulp has just the hint of a hard-edged and fragrant bite to it."pThis Berry is said to be a new kind that is a cross of two Berries brought together by winds from far away."gThis Berry is said to sense human emotions for the way it swells roundly when a person approaches."rThe flower grows at the tip of this Berry. It attracts Bug Pokémon by letting its stringy petals stream out."uIt is often used for pickles because of its very dry flavor. It can also be eaten raw for its provocative taste."yConsidered to have a speci